// LIMITATION P4: multimodule thin-link fails when the imported module
// carries more than ~10.2k assignment statements of this shape. This main
// imports a leaf with 10,400 assignments (52 functions x 200, generated by
// p4_gen_fixture.py; each function is individually under the P1 per-function
// cap). Expected: prints 400, as the control does.
// Observed (2026-08-02, Madaros v0.80.0): lowering and IR merge succeed,
// then native-binary write fails:
//   Error: Failed to write native binary to .../main.elf rc=19
//   error: multimodule native thin-link compilation failed
// Round-6 reported the threshold as ~24k on its (differently-shaped)
// generated module; the threshold is statement-shape-dependent.
// Related: the same 52 functions pasted into ONE module crash the
// single-module compiler path with SIGSEGV instead (see REPORT.md P4).
// Control: p4_thinlink_control_main.sio (10,200) builds and prints 400.
use p4_thinlink_leaf::{f0, f1}
fn main() -> i32 with IO {
    println(f0() + f1())
    return 0
}
